+# VOICE SERVICE ARCHITECTURE — Zero-Compute High-Fidelity Bangla TTS (#540)
+
+> Satellite: `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-command` · Layer 2 (Tools / Workers /
+> Sidecars) · Priority P2 · Status: implemented, offline-verified (33 tests)
+> plus a live protocol probe (17,424-byte MP3, 25 streamed chunks).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why zero-compute (philosophy compliance)
+
+Deploying local neural TTS engines (Coqui, XTTS, KittenTTS) costs 2–8 GB of
+RAM/VRAM plus gigabytes of model weights — a direct violation of the SupremeAI
+doctrine:
+
+- **"Simple + effective > clever + complex."**
+- **"Complexity must earn its existence."**
+- **"Incremental improvement > premature scale."**
+
+The voice service instead **leases** synthesis over the Microsoft Edge Neural
+TTS WebSocket protocol through the tiny `edge-tts` client: **0 MB of model
+weights, 0 GPU, 0 MB resident bloat**. The satellite's stdlib-only runtime
+core (boundary limit 5) is preserved: `edge_tts` is imported **lazily** and
+only when real synthesis is requested. Without it the service degrades
+**loudly** (`VoiceServiceUnavailable`) — the exact Redis/KillSwitch precedent
+(`KillSwitchUnavailable`) — never silently.
+
+## 2. Component map
+
+```
+src/services/voice_service.py   async adapter: validation → cache → leased stream → MP3 bytes
+src/utils/audio_cache.py        ephemeral SHA-256 cache (memory LRU or temp-file backend)
+src/telegram_bot.py             /voice command + /voiceon|/voiceoff toggle + sendVoice transport
+skills/voice/bangla_voice.yaml  skill package contract (speak_bangla)
+tests/test_voice_service.py     33 offline unit tests (fakes + injected clocks)
+```
+
+## 3. Voice catalog (Bangla-first)
+
+| Voice id | Gender | Dialect | Role |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `bn-BD-PradeepNeural` | male | bn-BD | authoritative system broadcasts / status reports (default) |
+| `bn-BD-NabanitaNeural` | female | bn-BD | interactive conversational assistant |
+| `bn-IN-BashkarNeural` | male | bn-IN | alternate dialect fallback |
+| `bn-IN-TanishaaNeural` | female | bn-IN | alternate dialect fallback |
+
+Short aliases (`pradeep`, `nabanita`, `bashkar`, `tanishaa`, case-insensitive)
+resolve to canonical ids; anything else is rejected fail-closed
+(`VoiceRequestError`). Rate (`"+10%"`, `"-5%"`) and pitch (`"+5Hz"`,
+`"-10Hz"`) are regex-validated before touching the wire.
+
+## 4. Data flow
+
+```
+/voice <text>                /status (voice alerts enabled)
+     │                             │
+     ▼                             ▼
+CommandRouter ── synthesize_voice(text) ──► sync_voice_synthesizer
+     │                                        │ asyncio.run(...)
+     ▼                                        ▼
+VoiceOutcome ◄──────────────────────── VoiceService.synthesize(VoiceRequest)
+     │                                        │
+     │                              ① cache.get(sha256(text|voice|rate|pitch))
+     │                              ② miss → edge_tts.Communicate(...).stream()
+     │                              ③ chunks yielded AND buffered → cache.put
+     │                              ④ VoiceResult(audio, cached, chunk_count)
+     ▼                                        ▼
+BotReply(text, voice_audio=bytes) ──► StdlibTelegramTransport.send_voice()
+                                        (multipart sendVoice, stdlib only)
+```
+
+Key decisions:
+
+- **Streaming**: `VoiceService.stream()` yields MP3 chunks as they arrive;
+  chunks are simultaneously buffered so the cache is populated **without a
+  second network round-trip**.
+- **Cache key** = `SHA-256(text · voice · rate · pitch)` with a `\x1f` unit
+  separator between fields (no field-boundary bleed: `key("ab","c")` ≠
+  `key("a","bc")`). A hit is byte-equivalent to a fresh synthesis by
+  construction.
+- **Ephemeral by contract**: memory backend (LRU `max_entries`, TTL via
+  injectable clock) or temp-file backend (`tempfile.mkdtemp`, wiped on
+  `close()`). Nothing persists across reboots; the cache is never a source
+  of truth.
+- **Timeouts everywhere** (guard doctrine): `connect_timeout=10`,
+  `receive_timeout=30` into the protocol client **plus** a 60 s wall-clock
+  `asyncio.wait_for` guard around the whole synthesis.
+- **Text cap**: 4,000 chars — one Telegram voice note, not an audiobook.
+
+## 5. Telegram surface additions
+
+| Command | Behavior |
+|---|---|
+| `/voice <text>` | synthesize Bangla voice note (default Pradeep), upload via sendVoice; on failure replies `🔊 voice synthesis failed: <reason>` (loud, no crash) |
+| `/voiceon` | status summaries now carry a Bangla voice note |
+| `/voiceoff` | disable status voice notes |
+| `/status` (voice on) | text runway first, then `build_voice_status_summary()` → deterministic Bangla phrase → voice note; synthesis failure appends a warning line, text always flows |
+
+RBAC is inherited: `/voice` from a non-superadmin chat is denied before any
+synthesis callable is invoked (test-enforced).
+
+Deterministic summary phrase (cache-friendly — the exact phrase from the
+issue): `সিস্টেম সম্পূর্ণ স্বাভাবিক আছে। কন্ট্রোল টাওয়ার সংযুক্ত আছে।`
+
+## 6. Error taxonomy (loud, specific, never silent)
+
+| Class | Raised when | User-visible |
+|---|---|---|
+| `VoiceRequestError` | empty/oversized text, unknown voice, malformed rate/pitch | `invalid request: …` |
+| `VoiceServiceUnavailable` | optional `edge_tts` not installed | `service unavailable: … run: pip3 install edge-tts` |
+| `VoiceSynthesisError` | protocol failure, timeout, zero-byte output | `voice synthesis failed: …` |
+
+`sync_voice_synthesizer()` never raises — every failure becomes a
+`VoiceOutcome(error=…)` so the Telegram poll loop survives.
+
+## 7. Skill contract (skills/voice/bangla_voice.yaml)
+
+```yaml
+function: speak_bangla
+signature: speak_bangla(text: str, voice: str = "bn-BD-PradeepNeural") -> bytes
+```
+
+Implemented verbatim as `command/services/voice_service.py::speak_bangla`
+(async; returns MP3 bytes). Optional dependency declared `edge-tts`.
+
+## 8. Verification contract (3-tier)
+
+```bash
+# Tier 1 — reflection
+git grep -n "edge_tts\|bn-BD-PradeepNeural" src/
+# Tier 2 — boot smoke
+python3 -c "import edge_tts; print('Edge-TTS ready')"
+# Tier 3 — unit suite (contract minimum 8; suite ships 33)
+python3 -m pytest tests/test_voice_service.py -v
+```
+
+Evidence (local, pre-landing):
+
+- Tier 3: **33/33 passed** offline + **15/15 seed regression**
+  (`tests/test_command_foundation.py`) — backward compatibility intact.
+- Satellite-layout parity: the suite passes with `src.*` imports too
+  (dual-import shim, same convention as the seed test).
+- Live protocol probe: `bn-BD-PradeepNeural` × "সিস্টেম সম্পূর্ণ স্বাভাবিক
+  আছে" → 17,424-byte MP3 (valid frame-sync), 25 streamed chunks; second
+  call served from cache (`cached=True`); `bn-BD-NabanitaNeural` with
+  `rate="+10%", pitch="+5Hz"` → 18,432-byte MP3.
+
+## 9. Boundary-limit compliance
+
+| Limit | Compliance |
+|---|---|
+| 1. Secrets env-only | no tokens/keys anywhere; transport reads `CommandConfig` (redacted repr) |
+| 2. Explicit timeouts | every protocol/HTTP call carries one (§4) |
+| 3. UTF-8, LF | Bangla strings are UTF-8; repo LF endings |
+| 4. Fail-closed input | regex-validated params, unknown voices rejected, oversized text rejected |
+| 5. Stdlib-only core | `edge_tts` optional + lazy + loud degradation |
+| 6. Augment, never bypass | voice is a presentation layer; all authority remains the Superadmin + Tower |
